text:
marie: Quick sync — I'm putting together a reproducible 429 guide we can run in CI. Draft PR: https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/4567. Need SDK snippet changes + a tiny load script. Anyone free to review tonight?

sam: I can take the SDK snippet edits. Are we changing the client retry defaults or just adding an explicit example showing backoff?

priya: Examples should demonstrate exponential backoff + jitter. Also add a small section that shows how to trim context to avoid token overflows causing timeouts. Quick note: include when to prefer client-side pacing vs server-side rate-limit handling.

rick: I'll add a minimal k6 script to the examples folder that reproduces short burst 429s. Plan: 200 vus for 20s then ramp down. Will add a comment about model vs account-level rate-limit behavior.

zoe: Heads up — I moved the 'rate-limits' anchor in the sidebar yesterday, so the PR's link to the table 404s. I'll paste the new link in a sec.

ci-bot: docs-ci: PR #4567 build queued

ci-bot: docs-ci: PR #4567 build passed (checks: lint, link-check, site-build)

sam: For SDK snippets, let's show both: minimal retry (pseudo code) and full recommended pattern. E.g.

```
// pseudo
await client.request({ ... });
// on 429 -> retry with backoff + random jitter
```

priya: Also add the 'when to fall back' bullet: lower-fidelity model variant or cached answer. Show config JSON for a fallback policy.

rick: Pasting k6 snippet I'll add to pr/examples/burst-test.js:

```
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';

export default function () {
  http.post('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'x'.repeat(2000) }), { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer $TOKEN' } });
  sleep(0.01);
}
```

zoe: New link for rate-limits table: https://docs.redwood.ai/reference/rate-limits#limits-table — update done in PR.

marie: Awesome. @sam please add the SDK snippets to the PR, @rick add the k6 file, @priya write the 'when to fallback' paragraph. I'll do a final pass for tone + examples. Goal: merge tomorrow morning. :rocket:

sam: On it. Will ping when snippet commit is up.

rick: k6 file pushed to branch. PR now has demo script and a short README for running locally.

marie: CI green and link checks passing. Scheduling merge for 08:30 PT tomorrow unless any blockers.

zoe: One small nit — update the wording in the context-trim section to call out 'truncate from the left' as the preferred approach for chat histories.

marie: noted, will include that. Thanks everyone :wave:
